# LF in the working tree, on every platform.
#
# Prettier's `endOfLine` defaults to "lf", and `format:check` is the FIRST step
# of the gate. Without this file a clone on a Windows machine with the default
# `core.autocrlf=true` checks out CRLF and fails that step on every file in the
# repo — a sibling counted 248 on a clone whose tree was byte-clean against
# HEAD. The repair looks like `prettier --write .`, which rewrites the whole
# repo into a diff that hides whatever was actually being worked on.
#
# The failure is worse than the gate step that finds it: Vite's shebang strip
# matches `#!...\n` only, so `scripts/*.mjs` checked out as
# `#!/usr/bin/env node\r\n` fail to PARSE, and every test that imports a
# script fails naming the script rather than anything it asserts.
#
# `text=auto` so git still keeps binaries out of it; `eol=lf` so the checkout
# matches what the gate demands rather than what the platform prefers.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Decks and images are bytes. Normalising them corrupts them. Declared rather
# than left to git's binary heuristic, which is good and is still a guess.
*.pptx binary
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
